(window.IND_GITA_V = window.IND_GITA_V || {})[4] = [{"v":1,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":"श्री भगवानुवाच","spp":"before","sa":"इमं विवस्वते योगं प्रोक्तवानहमव्ययम् ।\nविवस्वान् मनवे प्राह मनुरिक्ष्वाकवेऽब्रवीत् ॥","iast":"imaṃ vivasvate yogaṃ proktavānahamavyayam |\nvivasvān manave prāha manurikṣvākave’bravīt ||","read":"imam vivasvate yogam proktavaanahamavyayam |\nvivasvaan manave praaha manurikshvaakave'braveet ||","spli":"śrī bhagavānuvāca","splr":"shree bhagavaanuvaacha","en":"The Blessed Lord said: This imperishable yoga I declared to Vivasvân; Vivasvân taught it to Manu; Manu to Ikshvâku told it.","en2":"I told this imperishable Yoga to Vivasvat; Vivasvat told it to Manu; (and) Manu told it to Ikshvâku:","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":2,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"एवं परम्पराप्राप्तमिमं राजर्षयो विदुः ।\nस कालेनेह महता योगो नष्टः परन्तप ॥","iast":"evaṃ paramparāprāptamimaṃ rājarṣayo viduḥ |\nsa kāleneha mahatā yogo naṣṭaḥ parantapa ||","read":"evam paramparaapraaptamimam raajarshayo viduh |\nsa kaaleneha mahataa yogo nashtah parantapa ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"This, handed on down the line, the King-Sages knew. This yoga by great efflux of time decayed in the world, O Parantapa.","en2":"Thus handed down in regular succession, the royal sages knew it. This Yoga, by long lapse of time, declined in this world, O burner of foes.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":3,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"स एवायं मया तेऽद्य योगः प्रोक्तः पुरातनः ।\nभक्तोऽसि मे सखा चेति रहस्यं ह्येतदुत्तमम् ॥","iast":"sa evāyaṃ mayā te’dya yogaḥ proktaḥ purātanaḥ |\nbhakto’si me sakhā ceti rahasyaṃ hyetaduttamam ||","read":"sa evaayam mayaa te'dya yogah proktah puraatanah |\nbhakto'si me sakhaa cheti rahasyam hyetaduttamam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"This same ancient yoga hath been to-day declared to thee by Me, for thou art My devotee and My friend; it is the supreme Secret.","en2":"I have this day told thee that same ancient Yoga, (for) thou art My devotee, and My friend, and this secret is profound indeed.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":4,"sp":"arjuna","spm":null,"spl":"अर्जुन उवाच","spp":"before","sa":"अपरं भवतो जन्म परं जन्म विवस्वतः ।\nकथमेतद्विजानीयां त्वमादौ प्रोक्तवानिति ॥","iast":"aparaṃ bhavato janma paraṃ janma vivasvataḥ |\nkathametadvijānīyāṃ tvamādau proktavāniti ||","read":"aparam bhavato janma param janma vivasvatah |\nkathametadvijaaneeyaam tvamaadau proktavaaniti ||","spli":"arjuna uvāca","splr":"arjuna uvaacha","en":"Arjuna said: Later was Thy birth, earlier the birth of Vivasvân; how then am I to understand that Thou declaredst it in the beginning?","en2":"Later was Thy birth, and that of Vivasvat prior; how then should I understand that Thou toldest this in the beginning?","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":5,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":"श्री भगवानुवाच","spp":"before","sa":"बहूनि मे व्यतीतानि जन्मानि तव चार्जुन ।\nतान्यहं वेद सर्वाणि न त्वं वेत्थ परन्तप ॥","iast":"bahūni me vyatītāni janmāni tava cārjuna |\ntānyahaṃ veda sarvāṇi na tvaṃ vettha parantapa ||","read":"bahooni me vyateetaani janmaani tava chaarjuna |\ntaanyaham veda sarvaani na tvam vettha parantapa ||","spli":"śrī bhagavānuvāca","splr":"shree bhagavaanuvaacha","en":"The Blessed Lord said: Many births have been left behind by Me and by thee, O Arjuna. I know them all, but thou knowest not thine, O Parantapa.","en2":"Many are the births that have been passed by Me and thee, O Arjuna. I know them all, whilst thou knowest not, O scorcher of foes.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":6,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अजोऽपि सन्नव्ययात्मा भूतानामीश्वरोऽपि सन् ।\nप्रकृतिं स्वामधिष्ठाय संभवाम्यात्ममायया ॥","iast":"ajo’pi sannavyayātmā bhūtānāmīśvaro’pi san |\nprakṛtiṃ svāmadhiṣṭhāya saṃbhavāmyātmamāyayā ||","read":"ajo'pi sannavyayaatmaa bhootaanaameeshvaro'pi san |\nprakritim svaamadhishthaaya sambhavaamyaatmamaayayaa ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Though unborn, the imperishable Self, and also the Lord of all beings, brooding over nature which is Mine own, yet I am born through My own Power.","en2":"Though I am unborn, of changeless nature and Lord of beings, yet subjugating My Prakriti, I come into being by My own Mâyâ.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":7,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यदा यदा हि धर्मस्य ग्लानिर्भवति भारत ।\nअभ्युत्थानमधर्मस्य तदाऽऽत्मानं सृजाम्यहम् ॥","iast":"yadā yadā hi dharmasya glānirbhavati bhārata |\nabhyutthānamadharmasya tadā’’tmānaṃ sṛjāmyaham ||","read":"yadaa yadaa hi dharmasya glaanirbhavati bhaarata |\nabhyutthaanamadharmasya tadaa''tmaanam srijaamyaham ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Whenever there is decay of righteousness, O Bhârata, and there is exaltation of unrighteousness, then I Myself come forth;","en2":"Whenever, O descendant of Bharata, there is decline of Dharma, and rise of Adharma, then I body Myself forth.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":8,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"परित्राणाय साधूनां विनाशाय च दुष्कृताम् ।\nधर्मसंस्थापनार्थाय संभवामि युगे युगे ॥","iast":"paritrāṇāya sādhūnāṃ vināśāya ca duṣkṛtām |\ndharmasaṃsthāpanārthāya saṃbhavāmi yuge yuge ||","read":"paritraanaaya saadhoonaam vinaashaaya cha dushkritaam |\ndharmasamsthaapanaarthaaya sambhavaami yuge yuge ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"For the protection of the good, for the destruction of evil-doers, for the sake of firmly establishing righteousness, I am born from age to age.","en2":"For the protection of the good, for the destruction of the wicked, and for the establishment of Dharma, I come into being in every age.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":9,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"जन्म कर्म च मे दिव्यमेवं यो वेत्ति तत्त्वतः ।\nत्यक्त्वा देहं पुनर्जन्म नैति मामेति सोऽर्जुन ॥","iast":"janma karma ca me divyamevaṃ yo vetti tattvataḥ |\ntyaktvā dehaṃ punarjanma naiti māmeti so’rjuna ||","read":"janma karma cha me divyamevam yo vetti tattvatah |\ntyaktvaa deham punarjanma naiti maameti so'rjuna ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"He who thus knoweth My divine birth and action, in its essence, having abandoned the body, cometh not to birth again, but cometh unto Me, O Arjuna.","en2":"He who thus knows, in true light, My divine birth and action, leaving the body, is not born again: he attains to Me, O Arjuna.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":10,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"वीतरागभयक्रोधा मन्मया मामुपाश्रिताः ।\nबहवो ज्ञानतपसा पूता मद्भावमागताः ॥","iast":"vītarāgabhayakrodhā manmayā māmupāśritāḥ |\nbahavo jñānatapasā pūtā madbhāvamāgatāḥ ||","read":"veetaraagabhayakrodhaa manmayaa maamupaashritaah |\nbahavo jnaanatapasaa pootaa madbhaavamaagataah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Freed from passion, fear and anger, filled with Me, taking refuge in Me, purified in the fire of wisdom, many have entered into My Being.","en2":"Freed from attachment, fear and anger, absorbed in Me, taking refuge in Me, purified by the fire of Knowledge, many have attained My Being.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":11,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"ये यथा मां प्रपद्यन्ते तांस्तथैव भजाम्यहम् ।\nमम वर्त्मानुवर्तन्ते मनुष्याः पार्थ सर्वशः ॥","iast":"ye yathā māṃ prapadyante tāṃstathaiva bhajāmyaham |\nmama vartmānuvartante manuṣyāḥ pārtha sarvaśaḥ ||","read":"ye yathaa maam prapadyante taamstathaiva bhajaamyaham |\nmama vartmaanuvartante manushyaah paartha sarvashah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"However men approach Me, even so do I welcome them, for the path men take from every side is Mine, O Pârtha.","en2":"In whatever way men worship Me, in the same way do I fulfil their desires: (it is) My path, O son of Prithâ, (that) men tread, in all ways.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":12,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"काङ्क्षन्तः कर्मणां सिद्धिं यजन्त इह देवताः ।\nक्षिप्रं हि मानुषे लोके सिद्धिर्भवति कर्मजा ॥","iast":"kāṅkṣantaḥ karmaṇāṃ siddhiṃ yajanta iha devatāḥ |\nkṣipraṃ hi mānuṣe loke siddhirbhavati karmajā ||","read":"kaankshantah karmanaam siddhim yajanta iha devataah |\nkshipram hi maanushe loke siddhirbhavati karmajaa ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"They who long after success in action on earth worship the Shining Ones; for in brief space verily, in this world of men, success is born of action.","en2":"Longing for success in action, in this world, (men) worship the gods. Because success, resulting from action, is, quickly attained in the human world.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":13,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"चातुर्वर्ण्यं मया सृष्टं गुणकर्मविभागशः ।\nतस्य कर्तारमपि मां विद्ध्यकर्तारमव्ययम् ॥","iast":"cāturvarṇyaṃ mayā sṛṣṭaṃ guṇakarmavibhāgaśaḥ |\ntasya kartāramapi māṃ viddhyakartāramavyayam ||","read":"chaaturvarnyam mayaa srishtam gunakarmavibhaagashah |\ntasya kartaaramapi maam viddhyakartaaramavyayam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The four castes were emanated by Me, by the different distribution of qualities and actions; know Me to be the author of them, though the actionless and inexhaustible.","en2":"The fourfold caste was created by Me, by the differentiation of Guna and Karma. Though I am the author thereof, know Me to be the non-doer, and changeless.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":14,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"न मां कर्माणि लिम्पन्ति न मे कर्मफले स्पृहा ।\nइति मां योऽभिजानाति कर्मभिर्न स बध्यते ॥","iast":"na māṃ karmāṇi limpanti na me karmaphale spṛhā |\niti māṃ yo’bhijānāti karmabhirna sa badhyate ||","read":"na maam karmaani limpanti na me karmaphale sprihaa |\niti maam yo'bhijaanaati karmabhirna sa badhyate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Nor do actions affect Me, nor is the fruit of action desired by Me. He who thus knoweth Me is not bound by actions.","en2":"Actions do not taint Me, nor have I any thirst for the result of action. He who knows Me thus is not fettered by action.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":15,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"एवं ज्ञात्वा कृतं कर्म पूर्वैरपि मुमुक्षुभिः ।\nकुरु कर्मैव तस्मात्त्वं पूर्वैः पूर्वतरं कृतम् ॥","iast":"evaṃ jñātvā kṛtaṃ karma pūrvairapi mumukṣubhiḥ |\nkuru karmaiva tasmāttvaṃ pūrvaiḥ pūrvataraṃ kṛtam ||","read":"evam jnaatvaa kritam karma poorvairapi mumukshubhih |\nkuru karmaiva tasmaattvam poorvaih poorvataram kritam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Having thus known, our forefathers, ever seeking liberation, performed action; therefore do thou also perform action, as did our forefathers in the olden time.","en2":"Knowing thus, the ancient seekers after freedom also performed action. Do thou, therefore, perform action, as did the ancients in olden times.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":16,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"किं कर्म किमकर्मेति कवयोऽप्यत्र मोहिताः ।\nतत्ते कर्म प्रवक्ष्यामि यज्ज्ञात्वा मोक्ष्यसेऽशुभात् ॥","iast":"kiṃ karma kimakarmeti kavayo’pyatra mohitāḥ |\ntatte karma pravakṣyāmi yajjñātvā mokṣyase’śubhāt ||","read":"kim karma kimakarmeti kavayo'pyatra mohitaah |\ntatte karma pravakshyaami yajjnaatvaa mokshyase'shubhaat ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"\"What is action, what inaction\"? Even the wise are herein perplexed. Therefore I will declare to thee the action by knowing which thou shalt be loosed from evil.","en2":"Even sages are bewildered, as to what is action and what is inaction. I shall therefore tell you what action is, by knowing which you will be freed from evil.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":17,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"कर्मणो ह्यपि बोद्धव्यं बोद्धव्यं च विकर्मणः ।\nअकर्मणश्च बोद्धव्यं गहना कर्मणो गतिः ॥","iast":"karmaṇo hyapi boddhavyaṃ boddhavyaṃ ca vikarmaṇaḥ |\nakarmaṇaśca boddhavyaṃ gahanā karmaṇo gatiḥ ||","read":"karmano hyapi boddhavyam boddhavyam cha vikarmanah |\nakarmanashcha boddhavyam gahanaa karmano gatih ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"It is needful to discriminate action, to discriminate unlawful action, and to discriminate inaction; mysterious is the path of action.","en2":"For verily, (the true nature) even of action (enjoined by the Shâstras) should be known, as also, (that) of forbidden action, and of inaction: the nature of Karma is impenetrable.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":18,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"कर्मण्यकर्म यः पश्येदकर्मणि च कर्म यः ।\nस बुद्धिमान् मनुष्येषु स युक्तः कृत्स्नकर्मकृत् ॥","iast":"karmaṇyakarma yaḥ paśyedakarmaṇi ca karma yaḥ |\nsa buddhimān manuṣyeṣu sa yuktaḥ kṛtsnakarmakṛt ||","read":"karmanyakarma yah pashyedakarmani cha karma yah |\nsa buddhimaan manushyeshu sa yuktah kritsnakarmakrit ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"He who seeth inaction in action, and action in inaction, he is wise among men, he is harmonious, even while performing all action.","en2":"He who sees inaction in action, and action in inaction, he is intelligent among men, he is a Yogi and a doer of all action.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":19,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यस्य सर्वे समारम्भाः कामसङ्कल्पवर्जिताः ।\nज्ञानाग्निदग्धकर्माणं तमाहुः पण्डितं बुधाः ॥","iast":"yasya sarve samārambhāḥ kāmasaṅkalpavarjitāḥ |\njñānāgnidagdhakarmāṇaṃ tamāhuḥ paṇḍitaṃ budhāḥ ||","read":"yasya sarve samaarambhaah kaamasankalpavarjitaah |\njnaanaagnidagdhakarmaanam tamaahuh panditam budhaah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Whose works are all free from the moulding of desire, whose actions are burned up by the fire of wisdom, him the wise have called a Sage.","en2":"Whose undertakings are all devoid of plan and desire for results, and whose actions are burnt by the fire of knowledge, him, the sages call wise.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":20,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"त्यक्त्वा कर्मफलासङ्गं नित्यतृप्तो निराश्रयः ।\nकर्मण्यभिप्रवृत्तोऽपि नैव किञ्चित्करोति सः ॥","iast":"tyaktvā karmaphalāsaṅgaṃ nityatṛpto nirāśrayaḥ |\nkarmaṇyabhipravṛtto’pi naiva kiñcitkaroti saḥ ||","read":"tyaktvaa karmaphalaasangam nityatripto niraashrayah |\nkarmanyabhipravritto'pi naiva kinchitkaroti sah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Having abandoned attachment to the fruit of action, always content, nowhere seeking refuge, he is not doing anything, although doing actions.","en2":"Forsaking the clinging to fruits of action, ever satisfied, depending on nothing, though engaged in action, he does not do anything.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":21,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"निराशीर्यतचित्तात्मा त्यक्तसर्वपरिग्रहः ।\nशारीरं केवलं कर्म कुर्वन्नाप्नोति किल्बिषम् ॥","iast":"nirāśīryatacittātmā tyaktasarvaparigrahaḥ |\nśārīraṃ kevalaṃ karma kurvannāpnoti kilbiṣam ||","read":"niraasheeryatachittaatmaa tyaktasarvaparigrahah |\nshaareeram kevalam karma kurvannaapnoti kilbisham ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Hoping for naught, his mind and self controlled, having abandoned all greed, performing action by the body alone, he doth not commit sin.","en2":"Without hope, the body and mind controlled and all possessions relinquished, he does not suffer any evil consequences, by doing mere bodily action.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":22,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यदृच्छालाभसन्तुष्टो द्वन्द्वातीतो विमत्सरः ।\nसमः सिद्धावसिद्धौ च कृत्वापि न निबध्यते ॥","iast":"yadṛcchālābhasantuṣṭo dvandvātīto vimatsaraḥ |\nsamaḥ siddhāvasiddhau ca kṛtvāpi na nibadhyate ||","read":"yadrichchhaalaabhasantushto dvandvaateeto vimatsarah |\nsamah siddhaavasiddhau cha kritvaapi na nibadhyate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Content with whatsoever he obtaineth without effort, free from the pairs of opposites, without envy, balanced in success and failure, though acting he is not bound.","en2":"Content with what comes to him without effort, unaffected by the pairs of opposites, free from envy, even-minded in success and failure, though acting, he is not bound.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":23,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"गतसङ्गस्य मुक्तस्य ज्ञानावस्थितचेतसः ।\nयज्ञायाचरतः कर्म समग्रं प्रविलीयते ॥","iast":"gatasaṅgasya muktasya jñānāvasthitacetasaḥ |\nyajñāyācarataḥ karma samagraṃ pravilīyate ||","read":"gatasangasya muktasya jnaanaavasthitachetasah |\nyajnaayaacharatah karma samagram pravileeyate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Of one with attachment dead, harmonious, with his thoughts established in wisdom, his works sacrifices, all action melts away.","en2":"Devoid of attachment, liberated, with mind centred in knowledge, performing work for Yajna alone, his whole Karma dissolves away.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":24,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"ब्रह्मार्पणं ब्रह्महविर्ब्रह्माग्नौ ब्रह्मणा हुतम् ।\nब्रह्मैव तेन गन्तव्यं ब्रह्मकर्मसमाधिना ॥","iast":"brahmārpaṇaṃ brahmahavirbrahmāgnau brahmaṇā hutam |\nbrahmaiva tena gantavyaṃ brahmakarmasamādhinā ||","read":"brahmaarpanam brahmahavirbrahmaagnau brahmanaa hutam |\nbrahmaiva tena gantavyam brahmakarmasamaadhinaa ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The Eternal the oblation, the Eternal the clarified butter, are offered in the Eternal the fire by the Eternal; unto the Eternal verily shall he go who in his action meditateth wholly upon the Eternal.","en2":"The process is Brahman, the clarified butter is Brahman, offered by Brahman in the fire of Brahman; by seeing Brahman in action, he reaches Brahman alone.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":25,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"दैवमेवापरे यज्ञं योगिनः पर्युपासते ।\nब्रह्माग्नावपरे यज्ञं यज्ञेनैवोपजुह्वति ॥","iast":"daivamevāpare yajñaṃ yoginaḥ paryupāsate |\nbrahmāgnāvapare yajñaṃ yajñenaivopajuhvati ||","read":"daivamevaapare yajnam yoginah paryupaasate |\nbrahmaagnaavapare yajnam yajnenaivopajuhvati ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Some Yogis offer up sacrifice to the Shining Ones; others sacrifice only by pouring sacrifice into the fire of the Eternal;","en2":"Some Yogis perform sacrifices to Devas alone, while others offer the self as sacrifice by the self in the fire of Brahman alone.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":26,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"श्रोत्रादीनीन्द्रियाण्यन्ये संयमाग्निषु जुह्वति ।\nशब्दादीन्विषयानन्य इन्द्रियाग्निषु जुह्वति ॥","iast":"śrotrādīnīndriyāṇyanye saṃyamāgniṣu juhvati |\nśabdādīnviṣayānanya indriyāgniṣu juhvati ||","read":"shrotraadeeneendriyaanyanye samyamaagnishu juhvati |\nshabdaadeenvishayaananya indriyaagnishu juhvati ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Some pour as sacrifice hearing and the other senses into the fires of restraint; some pour sound and the other objects of sense into the fires of the senses as sacrifice;","en2":"Some again offer hearing and other senses as sacrifice in the fire of control, while others offer sound and other sense-objects as sacrifice in the fire of the senses.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":27,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"सर्वाणीन्द्रियकर्माणि प्राणकर्माणि चापरे ।\nआत्मसंयमयोगाग्नौ जुह्वति ज्ञानदीपिते ॥","iast":"sarvāṇīndriyakarmāṇi prāṇakarmāṇi cāpare |\nātmasaṃyamayogāgnau juhvati jñānadīpite ||","read":"sarvaaneendriyakarmaani praanakarmaani chaapare |\naatmasamyamayogaagnau juhvati jnaanadeepite ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Others again into the wisdom-kindled fire of union attained by self-control, pour as sacrifice all the functions of the senses and the functions of life;","en2":"Some again offer all the actions of the senses and the functions of the vital energy, as sacrifice in the fire of control in self, kindled by knowledge.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":28,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"द्रव्ययज्ञास्तपोयज्ञा योगयज्ञास्तथापरे ।\nस्वाध्यायज्ञानयज्ञाश्च यतयः संशितव्रताः ॥","iast":"dravyayajñāstapoyajñā yogayajñāstathāpare |\nsvādhyāyajñānayajñāśca yatayaḥ saṃśitavratāḥ ||","read":"dravyayajnaastapoyajnaa yogayajnaastathaapare |\nsvaadhyaayajnaanayajnaashcha yatayah samshitavrataah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Yet others the sacrifice of wealth, the sacrifice of austerity, the sacrifice of yoga, the sacrifice of silent reading and wisdom, men concentrated and of effectual vows;","en2":"Others again offer wealth, austerity, and Yoga, as sacrifice, while still others, of self-restraint and rigid vows, offer study of the scriptures and knowledge, as sacrifice.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":29,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अपाने जुह्वति प्राणं प्राणेऽपानं तथापरे ।\nप्राणापानगती रुद्ध्वा प्राणायामपरायणाः ॥","iast":"apāne juhvati prāṇaṃ prāṇe’pānaṃ tathāpare |\nprāṇāpānagatī ruddhvā prāṇāyāmaparāyaṇāḥ ||","read":"apaane juhvati praanam praane'paanam tathaapare |\npraanaapaanagatee ruddhvaa praanaayaamaparaayanaah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Yet others pour as sacrifice the outgoing breath in the incoming, and the incoming in the outgoing, restraining the flow of the outgoing and incoming breaths, solely absorbed in the control of breathing.","en2":"Yet some offer as sacrifice, the outgoing into the in-coming breath, and the in-coming into the out-going, stopping the courses of the in-coming and out-going breaths, constantly practising the regulation of the vital energy; while others yet of regulated food, offer in the Prânas the functions thereof.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":30,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अपरे नियताहाराः प्राणान्प्राणेषु जुह्वति ।\nसर्वेऽप्येते यज्ञविदो यज्ञक्षपितकल्मषाः ॥","iast":"apare niyatāhārāḥ prāṇānprāṇeṣu juhvati |\nsarve’pyete yajñavido yajñakṣapitakalmaṣāḥ ||","read":"apare niyataahaaraah praanaanpraaneshu juhvati |\nsarve'pyete yajnavido yajnakshapitakalmashaah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Others regular in food, pour as sacrifice their life-breaths in life-breaths. All these are knowers of sacrifice, and by sacrifice have destroyed their sins.","en2":"All of these are knowers of Yajna, having their sins consumed by Yajna, and eating of the nectar—the remnant of Yajna, they go to the Eternal Brahman. (Even) this world is not for the non-performer of Yajna, how then another, O best of the Kurus?","en2r":"4.30-31","rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":31,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यज्ञशिष्टामृतभुजो यान्ति ब्रह्म सनातनम् ।\nनायं लोकोऽस्त्ययज्ञस्य कुतोऽन्यः कुरुसत्तम ॥","iast":"yajñaśiṣṭāmṛtabhujo yānti brahma sanātanam |\nnāyaṃ loko’styayajñasya kuto’nyaḥ kurusattama ||","read":"yajnashishtaamritabhujo yaanti brahma sanaatanam |\nnaayam loko'styayajnasya kuto'nyah kurusattama ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The eaters of the life-giving remains of sacrifice go to the changeless Eternal. This world is not for the non-sacrificer, much less the other, O best of the Kurus.","en2":"All of these are knowers of Yajna, having their sins consumed by Yajna, and eating of the nectar—the remnant of Yajna, they go to the Eternal Brahman. (Even) this world is not for the non-performer of Yajna, how then another, O best of the Kurus?","en2r":"4.30-31","rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":32,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"एवं बहुविधा यज्ञा वितता ब्रह्मणो मुखे ।\nकर्मजान्विद्धि तान्सर्वानेवं ज्ञात्वा विमोक्ष्यसे ॥","iast":"evaṃ bahuvidhā yajñā vitatā brahmaṇo mukhe |\nkarmajānviddhi tānsarvānevaṃ jñātvā vimokṣyase ||","read":"evam bahuvidhaa yajnaa vitataa brahmano mukhe |\nkarmajaanviddhi taansarvaanevam jnaatvaa vimokshyase ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Many and various sacrifices are thus spread out before the Eternal. Know thou that all these are born of action, and thus knowing thou shalt be free.","en2":"Various Yajnas, like the above, are strewn in the store-house of the Veda. Know them all to be born of action, and thus knowing, thou shalt be free.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":33,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"श्रेयान्द्रव्यमयाद्यज्ञाज्ज्ञानयज्ञः परन्तप ।\nसर्वं कर्माखिलं पार्थ ज्ञाने परिसमाप्यते ॥","iast":"śreyāndravyamayādyajñājjñānayajñaḥ parantapa |\nsarvaṃ karmākhilaṃ pārtha jñāne parisamāpyate ||","read":"shreyaandravyamayaadyajnaajjnaanayajnah parantapa |\nsarvam karmaakhilam paartha jnaane parisamaapyate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Better than the sacrifice of any objects is the sacrifice of wisdom, O Parantapa. All actions in their entirety, O Pârtha, culminate in wisdom.","en2":"Knowledge-sacrifice, O scorcher of foes, is superior to sacrifice (performed) with (material) objects. All action in its entirety, O Pârtha, attains its consummation in knowledge.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":34,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"तद्विद्धि प्रणिपातेन परिप्रश्नेन सेवया ।\nउपदेक्ष्यन्ति ते ज्ञानं ज्ञानिनस्तत्त्वदर्शिनः ॥","iast":"tadviddhi praṇipātena paripraśnena sevayā |\nupadekṣyanti te jñānaṃ jñāninastattvadarśinaḥ ||","read":"tadviddhi pranipaatena pariprashnena sevayaa |\nupadekshyanti te jnaanam jnaaninastattvadarshinah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Learn thou this by discipleship, by investiga tion, and by service. The wise, the seers of the essence of things, will instruct thee in wisdom.","en2":"Know that, by prostrating thyself, by questions, and by service; the wise, those who have realised the Truth, will instruct thee in that knowledge.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":35,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यज्ज्ञात्वा न पुनर्मोहमेवं यास्यसि पाण्डव ।\nयेन भूतान्यशेषेण द्रक्ष्यस्यात्मन्यथो मयि ॥","iast":"yajjñātvā na punarmohamevaṃ yāsyasi pāṇḍava |\nyena bhūtānyaśeṣeṇa drakṣyasyātmanyatho mayi ||","read":"yajjnaatvaa na punarmohamevam yaasyasi paandava |\nyena bhootaanyasheshena drakshyasyaatmanyatho mayi ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"And having known this, thou shalt not again fall into this confusion, O Pândava; for by this thou wilt see all beings without exception in the Self, and thus in Me.","en2":"Knowing which, thou shalt not, O Pândava, again get deluded like this, and by which thou shalt see the whole of creation in (thy) Self and in Me.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":36,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अपि चेदसि पापेभ्यः सर्वेभ्यः पापकृत्तमः ।\nसर्वं ज्ञानप्लवेनैव वृजिनं सन्तरिष्यसि ॥","iast":"api cedasi pāpebhyaḥ sarvebhyaḥ pāpakṛttamaḥ |\nsarvaṃ jñānaplavenaiva vṛjinaṃ santariṣyasi ||","read":"api chedasi paapebhyah sarvebhyah paapakrittamah |\nsarvam jnaanaplavenaiva vrijinam santarishyasi ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Even if thou art the most sinful of all sinners, yet shalt thou cross over all sin by the raft of wisdom.","en2":"Even if thou be the most sinful among all the sinful, yet by the raft of knowledge alone thou shalt go across all sin.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":37,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यथैधांसि समिद्धोऽग्निर्भस्मसात्कुरुतेऽर्जुन ।\nज्ञानाग्निः सर्वकर्माणि भस्मसात्कुरुते तथा ॥","iast":"yathaidhāṃsi samiddho’gnirbhasmasātkurute’rjuna |\njñānāgniḥ sarvakarmāṇi bhasmasātkurute tathā ||","read":"yathaidhaamsi samiddho'gnirbhasmasaatkurute'rjuna |\njnaanaagnih sarvakarmaani bhasmasaatkurute tathaa ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"As the burning fire reduces fuel to ashes, O Arjuna, so doth the fire of wisdom reduce all actions to ashes.","en2":"As blazing fire reduces wood into ashes, so, O Arjuna, does the fire of knowledge reduce all Karma to ashes.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":38,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"न हि ज्ञानेन सदृशं पवित्रमिह विद्यते ।\nतत्स्वयं योगसंसिद्धः कालेनात्मनि विन्दति ॥","iast":"na hi jñānena sadṛśaṃ pavitramiha vidyate |\ntatsvayaṃ yogasaṃsiddhaḥ kālenātmani vindati ||","read":"na hi jnaanena sadrisham pavitramiha vidyate |\ntatsvayam yogasamsiddhah kaalenaatmani vindati ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Verily there is no purifier in this world like wisdom; he that is perfected in yoga finds it in the Self in due season.","en2":"Verily there exists nothing in this world purifying like knowledge. In good time, having reached perfection in Yoga, one realises that oneself in one's own heart.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":39,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"श्रद्धावाँल्लभते ज्ञानं तत्परः संयतेन्द्रियः ।\nज्ञानं लब्ध्वा परां शान्तिमचिरेणाधिगच्छति ॥","iast":"śraddhāvām̐llabhate jñānaṃ tatparaḥ saṃyatendriyaḥ |\njñānaṃ labdhvā parāṃ śāntimacireṇādhigacchati ||","read":"shraddhaavaanllabhate jnaanam tatparah samyatendriyah |\njnaanam labdhvaa paraam shaantimachirenaadhigachchhati ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The man who is full of faith obtaineth wisdom, and he also who hath mastery over his senses; and, having obtained wisdom, he goeth swiftly to the supreme Peace.","en2":"The man with Shraddhâ, the devoted, the master of one's senses, attains (this) knowledge. Having attained knowledge one goes at once to the Supreme Peace.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":40,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अज्ञश्चाश्रद्दधानश्च संशयात्मा विनश्यति ।\nनायं लोकोऽस्ति न परो न सुखं संशयात्मनः ॥","iast":"ajñaścāśraddadhānaśca saṃśayātmā vinaśyati |\nnāyaṃ loko’sti na paro na sukhaṃ saṃśayātmanaḥ ||","read":"ajnashchaashraddadhaanashcha samshayaatmaa vinashyati |\nnaayam loko'sti na paro na sukham samshayaatmanah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"But the ignorant, faithless, doubting self goeth to destruction; nor this world, nor that beyond, nor happiness, is there for the doubting self.","en2":"The ignorant, the man without Shraddhâ, the doubting self, goes to destruction. The doubting self has neither this world, nor the next, nor happiness.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":41,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"योगसंन्यस्तकर्माणं ज्ञानसंछिन्नसंशयम् ।\nआत्मवन्तं न कर्माणि निबध्नन्ति धनञ्जय ॥","iast":"yogasaṃnyastakarmāṇaṃ jñānasaṃchinnasaṃśayam |\nātmavantaṃ na karmāṇi nibadhnanti dhanañjaya ||","read":"yogasamnyastakarmaanam jnaanasamchhinnasamshayam |\naatmavantam na karmaani nibadhnanti dhananjaya ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"He who hath renounced actions by yoga, who hath cloven asunder doubt by wisdom, who is ruled by the Self, actions do not bind him, O Dhananjaya.","en2":"With work renounced by Yoga and doubts rent asunder by knowledge, O Dhananjaya, actions do not bind him who is poised in the Self.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":42,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"तस्मादज्ञानसंभूतं हृत्स्थं ज्ञानासिनाऽऽत्मनः ।\nछित्त्वैनं संशयं योगमातिष्ठोत्तिष्ठ भारत ॥","iast":"tasmādajñānasaṃbhūtaṃ hṛtsthaṃ jñānāsinā’’tmanaḥ |\nchittvainaṃ saṃśayaṃ yogamātiṣṭhottiṣṭha bhārata ||","read":"tasmaadajnaanasambhootam hritstham jnaanaasinaa''tmanah |\nchhittvainam samshayam yogamaatishthottishtha bhaarata ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Therefore, with the sword of the wisdom of the Self cleaving asunder this ignorance-born doubt dwelling in thy heart, be established in yoga. Stand up, O Bhârata.","en2":"Therefore, cutting with the sword of knowledge, this doubt about the Self, born of ignorance, residing in thy heart, take refuge in Yoga. Arise, O Bhârata!","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null}];
